1
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to me.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,040
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:36,320
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:42,840
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

5
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

6
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,600
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

7
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:12,160
The burning steel masses too.

8
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

9
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

10
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,360
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

11
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:46,540
A female officer's big win: a bank robber
flattened with a one-armed shoulder throw.

12
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:48,880
Matoi-chan, you're amazing.

13
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:53,180
Now the number one woman
everyone at Katsushika Station wants to marry

14
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:56,380
is becoming a threat to Reiko-san's throne.

15
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:59,120
Matoi-chan is young and cute,

16
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,920
so it's only a matter of
time before I get overtaken.

17
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:05,420
As the senior who almost married Matoi-chan,

18
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:07,800
you must have mixed feelings, don't you?

19
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,580
Forget about that old story already.

20
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:14,500
Old? It was just the other day, wasn't it?

21
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,220
It was only a marriage for the money,
after all.

22
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,580
I can understand why
Ryo-chan wants to forget it.

23
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:23,020
Thanks to that,
Matoi-chan's popularity has skyrocketed.

24
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:27,420
Meanwhile, the senior officer
has proudly held onto the top spot

25
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:30,320
as the most unmarriageable
man for 12 years in a row.

26
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,280
Shut up!

27
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:34,140
Anyway, a wild filly like that woman

28
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:35,600
I'd be the one to turn down.

29
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,240
Sorry I'm not good enough for you, then.

30
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,080
Well, Matoi!

31
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:43,680
Hey.

32
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:45,200
Hello, Matoi-chan.

33
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:46,160
Hello.

34
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,660
It's a real gold coin!

35
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:55,200
Matoi and I love each other.

36
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,420
If we get married, we'd live off our
money for the rest of our lives, right?

37
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,140
You understand now, don't you?

38
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:07,020
This is the true face of Ryosuke, the man.

39
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,080
W-wait, Matoi, it's not like that!

40
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,080
My feelings aren't a lie.

41
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,520
I just wanted the treasure first,
that's all.

42
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,040
Goodbye.

43
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:20,100
Back then, well, that was...

44
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,940
I don't mind at all anymore.

45
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:26,800
You should mind a little.

46
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:28,940
Anyway, Kankichi.

47
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:31,220
I've got something I need you to do.

48
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:32,080
What is it?

49
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:39,260
Well, Grandma came over to the house, and
Gepard turned it down, I bet he'll refuse again.

50
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:47,720
You're going to lecture me about how the dorm guy is greedy for money or whatever, aren't you?
No, it's not like that. My computer's acting up and I'm in a real bind.

51
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:52,700
It's affecting my business too,
so I need it fixed fast.

52
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:59,140
If you feed me all the sushi I can eat as the repair fee,
I'll think about it.

53
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:00,880
Here we go again.

54
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:04,500
Since it's you, Ryo-chan,
that's an easy favor.

55
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:07,520
Alright,
I'll go first thing tomorrow morning.

56
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:11,600
I'm off duty too,
so I'll drive over and pick you up, Ryo.

57
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:13,240
Well then.

58
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:17,700
Ijiribashi Hakusen Nagashi

59
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,280
Look who it is.

60
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:32,460
Kankichi.

61
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:36,540
Don't come at me with
that face all of a sudden.

62
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,720
Says the one with the
face to talk about others.

63
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,220
Anyway,

64
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,280
fix my computer.

65
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:45,260
You barge in the second you arrive

66
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,440
At least serve some tea, damn it.

67
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,740
Shut up!

68
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,280
Looks like it's fixed, doesn't it?

69
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,880
Yeah, it was over capacity.

70
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:04,520
I added a hard disk and memory,
so it should be fine.

71
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,240
Look, Matoi.

72
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:10,480
As for Gepparuto,
to get sushi ingredients cheaply,

73
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,720
he's been spreading
networks all over the world

74
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:15,400
and trading over the internet, the bastard.

75
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:16,852
Thanks to that,

76
00:05:16,902 --> 00:05:21,040
our sushi has gotten a reputation as the
cheapest and most delicious place in Tokyo,

77
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:29,120
and for someone who only started using a computer three months ago,
you've done pretty well.

78
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:36,160
But with a small-capacity computer like this, it's going to crash.
And what is this?

79
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:40,300
What's this, Grandma?

80
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:47,000
Aaah! You even set up a
creepy homepage like this!

81
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:50,740
There are tons of
homepages for young people,

82
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,680
but there weren't any for old people,
so I made one.

83
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:56,120
I thought the idea was a good one, though.

84
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:00,040
That's why it freezes,
you keep making useless stuff like this.

85
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,460
Grandma.

86
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:07,300
Seconds!

87
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,540
What an appetite!

88
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,620
That Ryotsu guy doesn't know
the meaning of restraint.

89
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:14,300
Hello.

90
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:14,580
Hello.

91
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,060
Nakagawa, Reiko, welcome!

92
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:20,220
You two came too?

93
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,892
We were nearby for work,

94
00:06:23,942 --> 00:06:26,780
so we thought we'd grab some sushi too.

95
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:30,580
In that case, today's on me. Order away!

96
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,520
But...

97
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:36,060
Matoi always looks after us.
Don't hold back, eat up.

98
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,080
Please, senpai.

99
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,180
Ugh, I'm stuffed.

100
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:42,960
Thank you for treating
us to such a feast too.

101
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:48,560
Thank you, please come again.

102
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:54,580
If anything goes wrong with the computer, call me again.
Heh, the shop would go under if I had to ask you for every little thing.

103
00:06:56,100 --> 00:07:01,300
Well, that's true. Matoi,
are you going somewhere? Just to Ochanomizu.

104
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:05,520
Then hop in and come along. Please.

105
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,660
Well, it's a class reunion planning meeting.

106
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:16,640
Yes, it's been a year since we graduated,
so we decided to get everyone together.

107
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:18,960
So it's a long-awaited reunion, then.

108
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:19,520
Yeah.

109
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,280
What are those guys doing?

110
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,320
It's Hakusen Nagashi.

111
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,680
Hakusen Nagashi.

112
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,900
Right, they had a drama like that on TV.

113
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:37,560
On graduation day, they tie their sailor-suit
scarves together and float them down the river, right?

114
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,180
Yeah.

115
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,800
Hakusen Nagashi

116
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,740
In America,
we had rituals at graduation too.

117
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:57,360
One, two, three!

118
00:07:58,340 --> 00:07:59,520
It's like a movie.

119
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:02,280
Yeah, those kinds of rituals.

120
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:05,700
I got a thick dictionary
at my graduation, too.

121
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:12,700
It was heavy and bulky,
and carrying it home was such a pain.

122
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,560
So I just threw it into the stove.

123
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,680
After that, it became an annual ceremony.

124
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,700
That's not a ceremony.

125
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,240
That's just being bad.

126
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:26,140
Found one! A proper one, see?

127
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:27,200
Really?

128
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,500
Don't tell me you gave your
second uniform button to a girl?

129
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:35,260
It wasn't anything that flashy.

130
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:40,300
I carved something into
the desk for my juniors.

131
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:43,480
A warm message from a senior, you know.

132
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,860
That's just awful.

133
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,040
Isn't that just graffiti?

134
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:50,720
You didn't study and only did that stuff,
so that's why you're an idiot.

135
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,420
Shut up.

136
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:55,620
Excuse me, are you Mr. Jupiter?

137
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:58,340
It really is Mr. Jupiter.

138
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,740
Senior Jupiter!

139
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,580
We're Mr. Jupiter's juniors.

140
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:05,640
I see. Today was your graduation ceremony,
wasn't it?

141
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:08,900
Yes. I've been a fan of yours
since I entered high school.

142
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:13,200
I'll never forget the softball
Tokyo tournament final.

143
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,820
The final inning,
when we were trailing by one run.

144
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:21,580
Two outs, runner on second,
and the senior batting at the plate...

145
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:34,000
That walk-off home run
that turned the game around

146
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:37,680
Even now, just thinking about
it makes my heart flutter.

147
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,680
That home run is my treasure.

148
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:43,680
Matoi was apparently the
ace and cleanup hitter.

149
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:46,660
So that's why she's so strong.

150
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:50,940
If it's not too much trouble,
could I please shake your hand?

151
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:51,880
Sure.

152
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,220
I'm so moved!

153
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:58,940
Thank you so much!

154
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,080
I'm so happy!

155
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:05,000
Thank you so much!

156
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,120
Wow, she's so popular!

157
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:08,720
What do I do!

158
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,100
Thank you very much!

159
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,820
Senpai, good luck with your work!

160
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:14,720
Thanks!

161
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,060
Excuse me!

162
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,400
Yay!

163
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,240
Hey, celebrity!

164
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:23,040
Still, shaking hands between women

165
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,140
I'm used to it.

166
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:28,160
Our school was an all-girls school, so

167
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,640
I got Valentine's chocolates
and love letters all the time.

168
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:33,540
Matoi's kind of masculine

169
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:36,980
The current uniform is from Daiwa
University's affiliated school, right?

170
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:38,240
Yeah.

171
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:39,760
That's amazing.

172
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:41,860
What's so amazing about it?

173
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,160
It's a high-level school.

174
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,840
It's really hard to get into.

175
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,340
Look, you can see it from here, right?

176
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:52,920
Behind Nikolai Cathedral,
that's where the school's back side is.

177
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:58,120
Unbelievable, for someone from
the Ryotsu family to be smart.

178
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:03,800
What are you talking about? Ryo-chan's little
brother is a Tokyo University grad and a lawyer.

179
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:07,140
Kankichi has a brother like that?

180
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:11,400
He's just a bookworm lawyer
who's only good at studying.

181
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:15,360
Or rather, Kankichi was just too dumb.

182
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:19,480
Shut up! I had too many other talents.

183
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,660
You're the one who went to
such a good school, though.

184
00:11:22,660 --> 00:11:24,380
So why didn't you go to university?

185
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,381
That's right,

186
00:11:25,431 --> 00:11:29,560
If you went to Orin Affiliated, couldn't you
have moved up through the escalator system?

187
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:33,000
Well, I had my reasons.

188
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,480
Now I'm curious.

189
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:47,580
like he punched his homeroom teacher.

190
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:50,700
or that he gave the
principal a good thrashing.

191
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:54,180
Dressed in dark clothes like that,
he's clearly not a senior.

192
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:57,720
So what if I met a police
officer destined for me?

193
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,900
A destined police officer?

194
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:11,100
A destined police officer?
What's that supposed to mean?

195
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:14,240
That was the winter I was in high school.

196
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,400
Honestly, I was so surprised.

197
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,440
And then, when I saw it, it was even more...

198
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:23,060
I'm sorry.

199
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:24,340
Big bro, are you okay?

200
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:27,380
Oh no, I've gone and
broken my shoulder bone.

201
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,200
Don't touch me.

202
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:32,540
Looks like you need to go to the hospital.

203
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,660
Hey, lady,
how about covering my hospital bill?

204
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:36,540
No way.

205
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:41,100
Knock off the cheap act, mister.

206
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,500
What was that

207
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,660
Let me take a look.

208
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:48,380
Dadadada!
Hey, what do you think you're doing

209
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:52,020
Then the bones aren't broken.

210
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:55,575
Hey, you get some fancy suit
made and think you're hot stuff,

211
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:56,900
Hey, you bitch!

212
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,460
You brat!

213
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,280
W-what the hell are you?!

214
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,156
Isn't it obvious?

215
00:13:11,206 --> 00:13:14,260
Or do I look like a prince
on a white horse to you?

216
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:16,460
Take this!

217
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:27,580
You son of a bitch!

218
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:42,380
Young lady, your spirit is admirable,

219
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:44,940
but one wrong step and you
could get seriously hurt.

220
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:47,060
Hey!

221
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:50,500
Hey!

222
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:54,060
Is this yours?

223
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,840
Sorry about that.

224
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:59,660
Are you a police officer, Santa?

225
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:00,620
Now, now.

226
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:02,060
Damn it! Get lost!

227
00:14:10,460 --> 00:14:13,180
No, I'm staking out a certain case.

228
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:15,060
That's why you're dressed like that.

229
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:19,320
Um, what's your name?

230
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,020
Hmph, I'm not worth naming.

231
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,140
So cool.

232
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:31,060
Wow, it's like something
out of a movie or drama.

233
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:36,080
That police officer's arms
were so thick and strong.

234
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:38,900
I still remember.

235
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:42,600
Don't tell me, Matoi-chan,
you're into that police officer...?

236
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,320
You fell for him at first sight.

237
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:49,520
Don't say such out-of-character things.

238
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:53,860
Besides, whether that Santa's
police badge is even real or not...

239
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,940
So what happened after that?

240
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,900
Yeah, I thought maybe we'd meet again.

241
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:10,220
On snowy days, rainy days, stormy days,

242
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:13,280
I searched for him on this bridge,

243
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:15,780
but I never found him.

244
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:20,120
Wait, you did meet him? On graduation day?

245
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,060
How dramatic!

246
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:24,260
Fate really does exist, doesn't it?

247
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:29,540
After the graduation ceremony ended,
we all gathered here,

248
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:31,640
and we were about to do the Hakusen Nagashi.

249
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,060
So this is goodbye to high school life

250
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:37,980
But we'll all see each other
again at university, right?

251
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:44,600
Actually, I'm torn about
whether to go on to university.

252
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,920
Wait, really?

253
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:50,540
Of course it's a lie! You already passed the entrance exams,
didn't you?

254
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:51,560
Yeah, that's right.

255
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,940
Don't scare me like that.

256
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:55,420
No, that's not it.

257
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:59,380
That kid dropped their ball
onto the dangerous tracks!

258
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,520
The kid fell down!

259
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:06,660
What are you doing?

260
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:12,420
Grab onto this, grab onto this.

261
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:17,620
Hold on tight, hold on tight, hold on tight!

262
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:21,120
Move aside!

263
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,320
Yaah!

264
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:37,540
Police car!

265
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:38,220
Hang in there.

266
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,560
Who was that just now?

267
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,260
Got caught by the big sister.

268
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:46,720
It's okay now, alright?

269
00:16:47,620 --> 00:16:50,780
Police car!

270
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:58,920
Come on, pull yourself together, kid!
Spit out the water you swallowed!

271
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,320
Alright, you're safe now.

272
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,780
Then the police came right away.

273
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:15,840
Thank you, big sis, kendo mister.

274
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:16,460
Yeah.

275
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,080
Thank you so much.

276
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:19,920
Take care.

277
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:24,580
Hey, don't be reckless
just because you're a woman.

278
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:28,500
Jumping into a river in that outfit,
of all things.

279
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,380
So it really is you.

280
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:35,740
Thank you very much for your
cooperation in saving a life.

281
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:39,580
In that regard,
may I have your address and name?

282
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:43,360
Mark my words, the police will be
issuing you a certificate of commendation.

283
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:45,040
See you.

284
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,320
Please wait.

285
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:48,560
Because I'm a police officer.

286
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,580
Police officer

287
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:55,680
Were you perhaps dressed as
Santa Claus last December?

288
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:59,020
The police officer who was
on stakeout on Hijii Bridge.

289
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:03,120
I've forgotten all about
that from so long ago.

290
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:06,900
That police officer was really cool,
wasn't he?

291
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:10,980
He was wearing a kendo mask,
so what's cool about him?

292
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:13,340
Say no to violence!

293
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:17,780
Matoi, did you ever find out who
that police officer was in the end?

294
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:21,860
Yes, I tried to ask his name,
but then the reporters showed up.

295
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,480
I got surrounded and had my picture taken.

296
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:28,320
Interviews and coverage kept pouring in.
I was so surprised.

297
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:31,720
The next day, I was called to the police station
and given a certificate of appreciation, you know.

298
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:35,480
I felt that helping people was a good thing,

299
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:40,160
so I decided to enter society early
and take a job that helps people.

300
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:43,980
So I gave up going on to university
and became a police officer.

301
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:48,820
Yeah, I wanted to become a cool
police officer like that man.

302
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,040
That's so like you, Matoi.

303
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:55,260
But I wonder who that police
officer in the kendo uniform was.

304
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:57,340
I don't know his last name, though.

305
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,480
The police officer who was at the scene,

306
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:04,400
I heard someone say he's a man named
Ryotsu from the Katsushika station.

307
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:06,440
He was from the Katsushika station?

308
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:11,080
Yes, so when I was assigned
to the Katsushika station,

309
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:15,720
I thought I might be able to meet that
guy with a name like Ryo-something.

310
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:19,900
Is there anyone named Ryo at our station?

311
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:23,180
There's no Ryo,
but there's Ryoichi and Ryoji.

312
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:26,020
Ryoichi Hanamura and Ryoji Nakata, right?

313
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:28,560
But it wasn't either of those two.

314
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:31,600
I hope he's at our station.

315
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:32,640
Who?

316
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:35,280
Right there, in front of you.

317
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:40,580
Hey, I'm not Ryo, I'm Kankichi, you know.

318
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:41,993
Matoi-chan,

319
00:19:42,043 --> 00:19:45,760
didn't the officer at the scene say
"Ryo-san" from Katsushika station?

320
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:49,460
Yes, because I said "Ryo-san."

321
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:53,300
I thought it was his given name,
not his surname.

322
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,820
But it's not a citrus fruit, right?

323
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:59,540
A police officer who jumps into
a river with a kendo mask on

324
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:01,620
has to be Ryo-chan, there's no one else.

325
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:04,240
I remember! Senpai!

326
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:06,900
Last spring,
when you competed in the kendo tournament,

327
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,780
your mask got stuck, remember?

328
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:17,480
Right! I put a shape-memory alloy in the mask so it wouldn't loosen,
and then it wouldn't go back to normal!

329
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:24,280
I finally won, and the chief treated me to French food,
but I couldn't eat it properly because of the noodles.

330
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:27,980
In the end, I blended it into
mush and drank it through a straw.

331
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:35,980
And on the way back, when I got to the Kijiri Bridge,
some high school girls were making a fuss looking at the river below.

332
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:38,160
So I looked down too,

333
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:41,140
and a boy was about to
drown in the Kanda River.

334
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,460
I jumped into the river without thinking,

335
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:48,220
and wasn't there a high school
girl who jumped in with me?

336
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,900
That high school girl was Matoi-chan,
you know.

337
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:57,620
So that means Santa Claus was Ryo-chan too?

338
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:01,640
No, I don't think Santa was me.

339
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,840
W-wait, that's right!

340
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:06,275
No, during the winter bonus two years ago,

341
00:21:06,325 --> 00:21:10,420
didn't he dress up as Santa
to escape the debt collectors?

342
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:11,600
Figures.

343
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:15,041
Yeah, yeah.
Sure enough, while he was running away,

344
00:21:15,091 --> 00:21:18,980
he saved a high school girl
who was being harassed by yakuza.

345
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:22,240
Is Mr. Santa a police officer?

346
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:23,100
Well, yeah.

347
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:25,020
Damn, where did he go?

348
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:25,700
Shoot.

349
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:33,040
The one who was dressed as Santa was

350
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:36,520
not on a stakeout,
but escaping the debt collectors?

351
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:37,620
Yep.

352
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,160
No way...

353
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:43,580
My precious memory...

354
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:57,600
It's a nightmare.

355
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:02,100
Falling for this guy twice.

356
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:07,220
Well, thanks to him you became a police officer,
so that's good enough, isn't it?

357
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:09,380
It can't be helped, really.

358
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:10,400
Matoi.

359
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:12,360
Everyone.

360
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:14,900
You were taking so long,
so we came looking for you.

361
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:16,380
Thought so. You were here.

362
00:22:16,380 --> 00:22:18,500
How's university, everyone?

363
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:19,760
It's fun!

364
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:21,180
If it weren't for the exams.

365
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:23,380
Matoi, you don't regret it, do you?

366
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:25,440
Not going to university.

367
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:26,420
Yeah.

368
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:31,000
Anyway, we were in the middle of the Hakusen Nagashi at graduation,
weren't we?

369
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:35,460
Oh right, with that kid falling in the river,
we couldn't finish it then.

370
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:39,400
Hey, shall we finish
the Hakusen Nagashi now?

371
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:41,980
But we don't have the scarves!

372
00:22:43,580 --> 00:22:47,500
Why don't we do that?
That's a pretty good idea, for you.

373
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:54,220
"For you" is unnecessary.
Wait, did you save me here in high school?

374
00:22:54,220 --> 00:22:57,740
The Santa guy? Do you remember that?

375
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:05,120
Thank you so much for that time. I guess
I got carried away with my own image of

376
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:07,560
him, I think. Ahaha.

377
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:10,560
This reminds me of high school.

378
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:14,100
A year ago...
so this is like graduating safely, I guess.

379
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:16,380
It's a little short, but...

380
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:18,420
Okay, done!

381
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:20,840
Alright, let's go.

382
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:23,740
One, two, three!

383
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:45,720
I can believe in the day we'll meet again.

384
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:55,140
Goodbye, my student days.

385
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:20,460
An afternoon after rain,
as if someone is calling

386
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:27,140
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand

387
00:24:28,220 --> 00:24:34,320
That strange feeling I had back then

388
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:39,540
So on the arcade street's tiles,

389
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,360
I tried walking only on the black ones

390
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:53,580
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets

391
00:24:54,540 --> 00:24:57,620
the politicians with
their self-important faces

392
00:24:57,620 --> 00:25:00,920
and the aunties with their wobbling brows

393
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:06,540
Just turn around that corner, go on

394
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:11,760
You'll meet everyone, everyone

395
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:19,680
Over there is Kame-ari,
well surely Kame-ari is there

396
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:24,860
Come on, everyone, to our town!

397
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:26,480
Thank you.

398
00:25:30,340 --> 00:25:33,220
Kinjirō's having a baby?

399
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:37,860
So this uncle here is the
one who's going to be born.

400
00:25:37,860 --> 00:25:39,620
Somehow, that's moving.

401
00:25:39,620 --> 00:25:43,740
Just wait! Uncle Kankichi is coming now!

402
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:47,700
Next time, say hi to my dear big brother.

403
00:25:48,540 --> 00:25:50,860
That's Kameari over there.

404
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,300
It's surely Kameari.

405
00:25:55,340 --> 00:25:59,220
Come on, everyone, to our town!

406
00:26:00,260 --> 00:26:00,780
Thank you.

